  "result": "I found the cause and wrote a plan. I haven't changed any code yet because plan mode is on. I also couldn't submit the plan for approval: the plan-approval tool isn't available in this session.\n\n**Cause:** Every shell's completion (bash, zsh, fish, PowerShell) splits the command line with `split_arg_string` in `src/click/shell_completion.py:603`. That function uses Python's `shlex.shlex`, which by default treats `#` as the start of a comment and drops everything after it. So `cli a#b c` is read as `[\"cli\", \"a\"]` instead of `[\"cli\", \"a#b\", \"c\"]`, and completion works from the wrong arguments.\n\n**Plan** (saved to `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\shell-completion-gives-wrong-atomic-trinket.md`):\n1. **The fix:** in `split_arg_string`, add `lex.commenters = \"\"` after `lex.whitespace_split = True` so `#` is treated as a normal character.\n2. **Tests:** add three cases to `test_split_arg_string` in `tests/test_parser.py`:\n   - `\"cli a#b c\"` should give `[\"cli\", \"a#b\", \"c\"]`\n   - `\"cli #a\"` should give `[\"cli\", \"#a\"]`\n   - `\"cli 'a#b\"` (missing closing quote) should give `[\"cli\", \"a#b\"]`\n3. **Changelog:** 8.5.0 has already been released, so add a new \"Unreleased\" section to the top of `CHANGES.md` with a note about this fix.\n\n**How I'll check it:** run `pytest tests/test_parser.py tests/test_shell_completion.py`, then confirm directly that `split_arg_string('cli a#b c')` returns `['cli', 'a#b', 'c']`.\n\nTell me to go ahead and I'll make the changes.",
